{
  "about": "RLMesh v2 crypto interop vectors (design §8.8). All byte strings are hex. Every fixed input (static and ephemeral private keys, the Ed25519 secret, Sealed keys, Ni, Nr) is BLAKE2s-256 of the UTF-8 string 'rlmesh/v2 vector: <name>' with the name given in `inputs`. Handshake ephemerals are what the injected RNG returned, so each side's draw is listed. Generated by crates/rlmesh-session-core/tests/crypto_vectors.rs (RLMESH_REGENERATE_CRYPTO_VECTORS=1), from rlmesh_session_core::crypto; the same test cross-checks them with chacha20poly1305, ed25519-dalek, blake2 and snow directly. Sealed: nonce = kind || 3 zero bytes || seq u64 LE; AAD encrypted = header || lp(keyexpr), integrity-only = header || lp(keyexpr) || body with an empty plaintext. Signed: signature over lp(\"rlmesh/v2 signed\") || header || lp(keyexpr) || body. IK: Noise_IK_25519_ChaChaPoly_BLAKE2s, k_up and k_down are the raw split (first = initiator to responder). Pairing: Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_BLAKE2s with an empty prologue and empty payloads; key 1 = laptop to daemon (first split output).",
